ngs we heard today Putin said  today that Russia stands for  multi-polarity and for Traditional  Values  who was he speaking to today and I dare  say that his intended audience may not  have been sitting right there before him  in Moscow  uh definitely not so so um his audience  is actually sitting or his his hopes for  audience uh is sitting in America and so  basically if Vladimir Putin is in a very  tough spot right now because he's losing  the war  um he's losing the war primarily because  the ukrainians have been fighting so  well and also primarily because he's the  the ukrainians have been getting a huge  amount of military support from the  United States of America and of course  Western Europe but if if Putin can  somehow convince the United States not  to support Ukraine then he'll be in a  position where he can actually win the  war and so what is he doing right now  he's trying to um reach out to the  Grassroots of the far right in America  in hopes that in 2024  um with the next presidential election  uh there will be a Groundswell of  support not to have Ukraine be funded by  him America and so this is kind of a  almost a Hail Mary if you will because  he's doing so badly in the war  well there is this concern in the U.S if  Republicans win control of Congress in  the midterm elections next month that  that will be the beginning of the end of  of this incredible U.S military support  for Ukraine how much would you say that  Putin is counting on this GOP  um grenade to explode on Capitol Hill  come November  well it says  it's his only hope really because he  can't win the war militarily at the  moment um he's lost 65 000 troops  according to the ukrainians he's lost a  lot of territory he's taken the people  he's replaced are not experienced  soldiers they're getting bombed by uh  ukrainians using Western Equipment  and so he really is in a he's he's  really playing dice now he's just hoping  and praying that he can somehow make the  U.S not support him and I I don't think  that in the end I mean I think that  there's been a few words spoken by Uh  Kevin McCarthy but on the on the  Republican side Mitch McConnell is  directly contradicting Kevin McCarthy  and so  I I don't think that America is going to  pull out of their support for Ukraine  but that is Putin's only desperate hope  right now and you know for the first  time a majority of Russians say that  they favor opening peace talks with  Ukraine that is according to a poll by  The Independent lavada Center  um the greatest support for this is  among young adults who also happen to  oppose Putin's mobilization of  reservists the most did you see these  Trends reflected in any of Putin's  comments today  but Putin says he's open for negotiation  but the only problem with his  negotiation that he's open for is he  wants to negotiate to say that he gets  all the Ukrainian territory that he's  already occupied that's not negotiable  and so so everything that he's um I mean  he's now sounding like kind of a weak  desperate man saying he wants to  negotiate and getting various proxies to  say that there should be negotiation and  and getting people to criticize Ukraine  saying they're not negotiating of course  they're not negotiating on the terms  that he set out that the terms that that  should be negotiated are a full  withdrawal of Russia from Ukraine and of  course that's not even on the table as  far as Putin is concerned and Vladimir  Putin um today we saw this again he  continues to shower Chinese president Xi  Jinping with words of affection but this  often seems to be something like an  unrequited love uh Putin looking less  like a Russian Bearer and more like a  panda bear do you know can you explain  what what's going on here  well so when before this war started  Putin was in Beijing with the Xi Jinping  at the Olympics and he he probably  whispered in in Gigi Ping's ear  um this is going to be a three-day War  we're going to humiliate America and the