n's Playbook here by amplifying  this threat simply by talking about it  so much  you know uh the essence of deterrence is  trying to affect the thinking of your  adversary so they do or don't do what  what you want and Putin is clearly  throughout this uh this Invasion since  February 24th has been rattling his new  nuclear saber to try to impact uh the  actions of Ukraine the United States and  our European allies uh they're  conducting a another nuclear test  recently it was fairly standard but in  the context of the invasion of Ukraine  and Putin's comments it's concerning I  think we have no choice to talk about it  but I think the Bible instruction has  handled it roughly right delivering as  far as I can tell very serious messages  behind the scenes while being relatively  cool in public and saying there would be  catastrophic consequences but not being  too specific I think that's about the  right move Ukraine's president zielinski  today described Russian efforts to  capture the eastern city of bakmut as  crazy given the the high cost of this  attack  um and the little strategic value that  the city presents  um what do you make of a Russian  strategy at the moment  you know the the Russians have been uh  getting pummeled uh and have been uh  we've seen them getting routed and and  in in serious Retreat and the more we  learn about the state of their forces uh  it's just uh not good at all and all the  momentum has been with Ukrainian forces  is because of their agility the skill  the Western weapons that are being  provided and and the high morale and so  a Putin you know annexed these quote  unquote Annex these four regions uh even  as his forces didn't control all of them  and were Retreat and that's a very  awkward thing for Putin as he's trying  to make this look more successful than  it really is and engender fleeting  support within Russia and so there's  been this tension between Putin at the  political level and as military leaders  as military leaders are saying we have  to do an organized Retreat we're getting  pummeled here if we don't it's going to  look like what we've seen around kharkiv  and yet Putin didn't want that so you  have the Wagner group in there trying to  be more successful and so there's an  interest on Wagner's part to show more  success but the bottom line is this is  just a distraction I'd say the overall  narrative continues and that is momentum  on the Ukrainian side  Bradley Bowman with the foundation for  the defense of democracies Bradley as  always we appreciate your time valuable  analysis tonight thank you  thank you

